# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this React + Vite project following the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart).

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 as a production dependency
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with complete dependency tree

### 2. Code Changes
**Modified: `src/main.jsx`**
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react'`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<StrictMode>` wrapper, following the React/Vite integration pattern from the official documentation

## Implementation Details

The Analytics component was added to the root render function in `main.jsx`, which is the entry point of this React application. This placement ensures that analytics tracking is active across all pages and components of the application.

The implementation follows the official Vercel documentation for React/Vite projects:
- The `@vercel/analytics/react` package is used (framework-specific)
- The `<Analytics />` component is placed at the root level to track all page views
- No additional configuration is required for basic analytics functionality

## Testing & Verification

✅ **Build Test**: Successfully ran `npm run build` - build completed without errors
✅ **Linter Check**: Ran `npm run lint` - one pre-existing linting error unrelated to our changes (react-refresh/only-export-components warning that existed before this implementation)
✅ **Dependencies**: Lock file properly updated with all new dependencies

## Notes

- The pre-existing lint error (`react-refresh/only-export-components`) on line 9 of `main.jsx` was already present in the codebase before this implementation (confirmed by testing the original code)
- No test suite is available in this project
- Analytics data collection will begin automatically after deployment to Vercel
- Analytics must be enabled in the Vercel project dashboard for data collection to work

## Next Steps

After merging this PR:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel project dashboard (Analytics → Enable)
3. Analytics data will begin collecting automatically
